From 80d8d03031aa166cf818e271459def08242964b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: huzayfa <mamajanovhyzayfa@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 05:32:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Harden the administrator bootstrap and gate Phase 1 with
 real CI

Phase 1 hardening: real-Postgres CI for the admin bootstrap, a full
production compose stack split into pull/build/up phases with smoke,
log-error, log-secret and backup/restore gates, bats tests for the deploy
preflight, and a live probe of the published site.

bootstrap-admin rejects bcrypt cost factors outside 04-31 and the $2x$ prefix,
and refuses to promote an existing non-ADMIN account (STUDENT and TEACHER are
covered), so a typo in PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAIL can no longer escalate a student or
teacher to ADMIN. The oxlint config now actually enables
typescript/no-explicit-any and typescript/no-floating-promises with a lint job
behind them, and CI greps the literal passwordHash read from the database
instead of the $2[aby]$ pattern.

